FIXED 2026-06-10  BUG #1  TCar dangling Store.get  (Functions/TCar.py, board_visitors/run)
    On MaxWaitTime timeout the boarding process is interrupted but its pending
    carqueues[source].get() is NEVER cancelled. The dead get stays on the Store's
    get_queue (FIFO, ahead of the live car) and steals the next visitor that arrives,
    who is then never boarded or reactivated -> silently lost.
    MEASURED: 222 / 3031 car visitors lost in a baseline run. Worse at sparse nodes
    (each timed-out/empty car leaks another get).
    FIX: cancel the get on interrupt (see the get.cancel() pattern in TShuttleBus._board),
    or rewrite boarding with a single timeout race like the bus does.

FIXED 2026-06-10  BUG #2  Traffic-model self-jam / crawl speed  (Functions/Trafficflowmodel.py greenshields_speed)
    A vehicle adds its OWN pcu to an edge before computing its own travel time, and
    near jam density greenshields gives ~0 speed (rho_clamped = rho_max*0.9999, the
    "PLACEHOLDER fix crawling speed" line). The bus (bus_equivalent=3) alone exceeds
    rho_max on 51/221 edges -> a 2 s segment becomes ~25000 s. One-way bus trip blows
    up from ~210 s to ~7 h.
    MEASURED: only 80 / 2068 shuttle visitors completed; ~1988 stuck.
    (1 edge also self-jams a single car, rho_max < 1.)
    FIX: set a real minimum crawl speed (e.g. 5 km/h floor) instead of ~0, and/or do
    not count a vehicle's own pcu when computing its own edge travel time.

FIXED 2026-06-10  BUG #3  Arrival clock offset + off-by-one  (Functions/TVisitorGenerator.py)
    gamma.rvs returns ABSOLUTE arrival times (loc/shift ~66271 s = 18:24), but the code
    diffs them and yields the gaps starting at env.now=0, discarding the offset.
    RESULT: visitors arrive at sim-time 1..40104 s instead of in the 64800..86400 window.
    EventStartTime is ignored and arrivals are misaligned with background_density_update
    (which reads env.now as seconds-since-midnight). Also diff of N samples = N-1, so
    5099 visitors spawn instead of 5100.
    FIX: yield to each absolute time, e.g. wait (sample[i] - env.now); keep all N samples.

FIXED 2026-06-10  BUG #4  TShuttleBus shared self.path  (Functions/TShuttleBus.py run)
    self.path is an instance attribute shared by all n_buses processes; with n_buses>1
    (an experimental factor, Phase 7) concurrent buses overwrite each other's path.
    FIX: make path a local variable inside run().

!   BUG #5  Parking timing not modelled  (Functions/TCar.py)
    CAR['FindSpaceParkCar'] (600 s) and CAR['ParkingLotEntryDelay'] are never used; the
    PDL parking-entry + find-space delays are missing. parking_lot slot is acquired but
    never released (fine only because main uses a huge capacity placeholder).

!   BUG #6  No output logging yet (Phase 5) — sim produces no per-visitor/car/bus/segment
    data, so results can't be inspected/validated. Also means losses (BUG #1) are invisible.

!!  BUG #7  Current baseline capacity does not clear all generated visitors by midnight.
    After the 2026-06-10 correctness fixes an instrumented run generated all 5100 visitors,
    but only 3031 completed by 86400 s with 694 still in the shuttle queue and 1326 still
    in the ticket-scan queue. This is no longer caused by the shuttle self-jam bug; it means
    the scenario parameters (notably NumScanLanes=2 and n_buses=1) or the run horizon need
